25	 * The bundled subscription is a normal EmailSubscription, so once it points at a
26	 * domain the audited /dashboard/email flow (addMailbox, getEmailDnsRecords,
27	 * verifyEmailDomain, checkEmailDeliverability) manages mailboxes + DNS for THAT
28	 * domain unchanged. `EmailSubscription.hostingAccountId` is the new link that marks
29	 * which subscription is the bundled one and ties it to this account.
30	 *
31	 * QUOTA / SECURITY invariants preserved exactly:
32	 *   - ONE bundled subscription per hosting account. Its bundled EmailPlan's mailbox
33	 *     count == the hosting plan's `mailboxes`, so the existing per-subscription cap
34	 *     in addMailbox() IS the account's included-mailbox budget — no way to multiply
35	 *     the entitlement by spreading it over several domains.
36	 *   - GLOBAL domain dedup (one EmailSubscription per domain across ALL users — the
37	 *     2026-07-25 cross-tenant email-takeover fix) is enforced on both setup and
38	 *     re-point, using the identical query subscribeEmail/orderEmailHosting use.
39	 *   - EXTERNAL (real) domains are created external:true, verified:false — holding
40	 *     the row grants no power over the domain's mail until the customer proves DNS
41	 *     control; addMailbox()/retryMailboxProvision() refuse to touch Mailcow first.
42	 *   - FREE subdomains are created external:false, verified:true (we own the zone,
43	 *     exactly like an in-account domain in orderEmailHosting) and we best-effort
44	 *     auto-publish the records — the deliverability self-check surfaces the truth.
